            <div xml:id="d508">

                <pb facs="0424" n="412" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg412"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.20/604: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Liberia</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Hibbard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-08-05T19:00:00-04:00">August 5, 1942—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>192. Your 243, July 24, 6 p.m. War Department requested Colonel Wood to submit
                    recommendations regarding contents of your 243, July 24, 6 p.m. In his reply
                    Wood questioned the need of establishing a defense area at Cape Palmas but made
                    no reference to any approach by the British on the subject of sending radio
                    personnel to that district.</p>
                <p>Please confer with Wood and report exact nature of British inquiry and reply made
                    thereto. War Department appears to have no present intention of taking over Cape
                    Palmas for defense purposes.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
